# Builtin library — visible from every module, lowest precedence:
# a custom module's own definitions and environment win.
#
# The environment a running module is handed (viba-interpreter.md). Read as
# a type, `environ` is an Environment — that is what a module's `$env` slot
# asks for; read as computation, it is the real environment. `Environment` is
# a plain function of the environment and the sub-environment's name, which is
# how a module call hands a module its own — `$viba_path` is where its imports
# are looked up, and a child keeps the parent's — and `$tmp_sub_env` is the same
# thing under a name nobody chose, fresh every call. Both take the environment
# as their first argument, so nothing is bound to the environment they came
# from: `environ.sub_env << environ << "child"` is the same call as
# `$sub_env << environ << "child"` (viba-interpreter.md).
Environment =
    Object
  * $viba_path str
  * $sub_env (Environment <- $env Environment <- $sub_env_name str)
  * $tmp_sub_env (Environment <- $env Environment)

environ = Environment

# The marker that makes one argument be computed only if it is wanted
# (viba-interpreter.md).
#
# A slot written `CalledByNeed[T]` is the type T; what the marker says is how
# that one argument is given — not computed up front, but handed to the host as
# something it calls if and when it needs it. So a step that may not need an
# argument never computes it — an `if/else` that really takes one branch
# (branch.viba) — while every other argument of the same call is given as usual.
#
# The marker is the tag `$__called_by_need_tag_yanatutt__` — a name nobody may
# use — and `$arg` holds the type being marked. Every layer reads through it
# and sees T (viba/partial.py::by_need_type).
CalledByNeed[Arg] =
    Object
  * $__called_by_need_tag_yanatutt__ ()
  * $arg Arg
